-- title:
--   A 2-adic Eisenstein idempotent tower acting on J₀(p)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime. Equip `JZero p` — the group of degree-zero divisor classes modulo principal divisors of the function field `modularFunctionFieldBar p` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, i.e. the points of the Jacobian of the modular curve of level $p$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ — with the module structure over the abstract Hecke algebra `HeckeAlg` $=\mathbb Z[x_\ell:\ell\text{ prime}]$ given by `heckeModuleBar p`, in which $x_\ell$ acts through the geometric Hecke operator `heckeOperatorBar p ℓ`. Write $\pi$ for the ring homomorphism from `HeckeAlg` to `heckeLatticeAlgebra p ∅` obtained by composing `heckeEvalForms p 2`, which sends $x_\ell$ to $U_\ell$ when $\ell \mid p$ and to $T_\ell$ otherwise inside the Hecke algebra on weight two cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(p)$, with the map `latticeRestrictHom p ∅` restricting such an operator to the lattice of cusp forms all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are integers. Let $\mathfrak P$ be `eisensteinMaximalIdeal p 2`, the preimage under `eisensteinEval p` of the ideal $(2)\subset\mathbb Z$. The assertion is that there exists a family $te : \mathbb N \to$ `HeckeAlg` such that for all $m$: $\pi(te\,m)^2-\pi(te\,m)$ and $\pi(te\,(m+1))-\pi(te\,m)$ lie in the ideal generated by $2^m$ in `heckeLatticeAlgebra p ∅`; for all $m, M$, every $x$ annihilated by $\mathfrak P^M$ with $2^m x = 0$ satisfies $te\,m \cdot x = x$; and for every $m$ and every $y \in$ `JZero p` with $2^m y = 0$ there is an $M$ with $te\,m \cdot y$ annihilated by $\mathfrak P^M$.
--
--   This produces the $2$-adic Eisenstein idempotent of the weight two level $p$ Hecke algebra as a compatible tower of elements of the abstract polynomial Hecke algebra, together with the two properties of its action on $2$-power torsion of $J_0(p)$ that make it a projector onto the Eisenstein part. It is used in the study of the Hecke action on the Tate module and on inertia at $p$, in [`ModularCurve.exists_mem_inertiaSubgroupIn_tateModule_rep_ne_of_adjoin_tateHeckeRep_apply_ne_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_mem_inertiaSubgroupIn_tateModule_rep_ne_of_adjoin_tateHeckeRep_apply_ne_zero) and [`ModularCurve.exists_nsmul_generator_idempotent_tower_heckeAlg_tateModule_inf_pi_closure_inertia_smul_sub`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_nsmul_generator_idempotent_tower_heckeAlg_tateModule_inf_pi_closure_inertia_smul_sub).
